! Test v1.09.0 (4/4): geometry optimization under smearing (RFO
! internals path).  H2O PBE/STO-3G, Fermi sigma = 0.01 Ha.  The
! system is gapped, so the smeared optimum must coincide with the
! plain-PBE optimum: reference run agrees to 6e-8 in the optimized
! coordinates and 5e-9 Ha in the energy (the exp(-gap/sigma)
! occupation tail).  Expected (container reference): converges in
! 6 steps to (Angstrom block)
!   O1  z =  0.18897508,  H2  y = 0.77276815, z = -0.50503754
!   Total energy (F=E-TS): -75.240999448589
! The diatomic (Cartesian-BFGS) optimizer path is exercised by the
! LiH/PBE fermi sigma=0.05 twin (converges in 7 steps).
%method  PBE
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%smearing fermi
%smearing_sigma 0.01
*geometry angstrom
 O   0.000000    0.000000    0.117300
 H   0.000000    0.757200   -0.469200
 H   0.000000   -0.757200   -0.469200
*end
